    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>According to Free States legend (treated here as true), Joaquin Murietta was a Mexican immigrant to 1850s California whose wife was murdered by a mob, sending him on a killing spree that claimed over 120 lives and made him California's most notorious bandit. As a posse closed in, Christopher Houghton offered him an eternity of bloodshed instead of death; Joaquin's friends arranged a substitute corpse to be beheaded in his place (the pickled head toured California for decades before being lost in the 1906 San Francisco earthquake), and Joaquin took his place at Christopher's left hand, Blood Bound and utterly loyal.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>A cold-blooded killing machine as deadly as an @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.WaQFCEXFzv8YeAgX]{Assamite} assassin, Joaquin serves as Christopher's eyes, ears, and dagger in the outside world, traveling the globe for a century perfecting the art of death. He has a cheerful, psychotic sense of humor and a beautiful smile he reserves for the moment before he kills. Storytellers are urged to use him sparingly given his lethality.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire and Blood-Bound master: Christopher Houghton. Haven: wherever Christopher is. Influence: none held personally, only through his sire.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
